WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.469
Welcome to My Cyber Learning.

2
00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:04.000
Here's a quick tour.

3
00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:06.667
My Cyber Learning is a free,

4
00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:11.029
vendor-neutral library of the best cyber security podcasts, books,

5
00:00:11.079 --> 00:00:14.267
learning platforms and experts, all in one place.

6
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.702
Not sure where to start?

7
00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:18.051
Switch on MCL Picks.

8
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:22.166
These are our curator's hand-chosen favourites: the podcasts,

9
00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:26.483
books and platforms we'd recommend to anyone getting into cyber.

10
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:32.633
Use the tabs along the top to browse podcasts, books, platforms and experts.

11
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.838
Then narrow things down by topic and level.

12
00:00:36.888 --> 00:00:39.308
Choose threat intelligence and advanced,

13
00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:44.308
and you'll find respected shows like Discarded and Future of Threat Intelligence.

14
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:48.673
Search for anything you like,

15
00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:52.583
and sort podcasts by their latest episode to see what's new.

16
00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:58.883
Each card shows listener ratings, how often new episodes come out,

17
00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:02.050
the topics covered, and links to start listening.

18
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.442
Community votes are shown separately.

19
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.271
Tap the heart to save your favourites to My List.

20
00:01:08.321 --> 00:01:11.785
Create a free account with a passkey, no password needed,

21
00:01:11.835 --> 00:01:14.375
and your list follows you to every device.

22
00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:19.455
At the top of My List, This week shows new episodes from your podcasts,

23
00:01:19.505 --> 00:01:23.788
the week's briefing stories in your topics, and a podcast to fill a gap.

24
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:26.676
Tick the weekly update in your account settings,

25
00:01:26.726 --> 00:01:29.383
and it arrives by email every Monday morning.

26
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:34.641
Your list also builds a learning map: everything you've saved, by type,

27
00:01:34.691 --> 00:01:37.404
and how many security topics you've covered.

28
00:01:37.454 --> 00:01:42.364
Topics you haven't explored yet are suggested below, with an MCL Pick for each,

29
00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:43.933
ready to save in one tap.

30
00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:45.891
Every morning,

31
00:01:45.941 --> 00:01:51.010
the Daily Briefing sums up the latest cyber security news from the leading news

32
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.408
podcasts, with the top stories first.

33
00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:57.827
Subscribe, and it lands in your inbox at half past eight.

34
00:01:57.877 --> 00:02:02.767
It's the easiest way to start your day up to speed with the latest cyber news.

35
00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.263
Spot a broken link?

36
00:02:05.313 --> 00:02:07.867
Tap the red flag to let us know.

37
00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.440
And if you know a great resource we're missing, suggest it.

38
00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:16.483
For books, just enter the ISBN and we'll fill in the details for you.

39
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.315
And to keep up with the site itself, open What's New.

40
00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:26.375
A small dot on the menu tells you when there's something new to see.

41
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.638
This is a cyber security site, so privacy and security are built in.

42
00:02:32.688 --> 00:02:36.510
You sign in with a passkey, so there's no password to steal.

43
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.672
Accounts and email addresses are optional, there are no ads or tracking cookies,

44
00:02:41.722 --> 00:02:46.448
our keys are kept encrypted, and we follow both UK and EU GDPR principles,

45
00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:48.900
keeping only the minimum data we need.

46
00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:54.317
Start exploring today, at my cyber learning dot co dot UK.

